      "text": [
        " : سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اَللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنْ رَجُلٍ يَحُجُّ بِدَيْنٍ وَ قَدْ حَجَّ حَجَّةَ اَلْإِسْلاَمِ قَالَ «نَعَمْ إِنَّ اَللَّهَ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ سَيَقْضِي عَنْهُ إِنْ شَاءَ اَللَّهُ تَعَالَى»."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2901 - It was narrated from Ya'qub ibn Shu'ayb, who said:\nI asked Abu Abdullah (as) about a man who performs Hajj with borrowed money and has already performed the Hajj of Islam.\nImam (as) said: \"Yes, and Allah (swt), the Exalted, will settle his debt, God willing.\""
        ]
      }
